#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cotangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56e18e89-aea2-59f5-a0f0-d5e526fec283" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33\\,126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287900} {:answer/id #uuid "e04267de-99ae-5fee-81f0-8d487adab2a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,278" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287901} {:answer/id #uuid "901ac479-663f-526a-bda7-0095c518b84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37\\,563" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287902} {:answer/id #uuid "8a42f3d4-3930-592e-951e-dd0415c135c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35\\,986" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287903} {:answer/id #uuid "a5552214-ac45-5197-81e7-05d92511937d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "43\\,245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "901ac479-663f-526a-bda7-0095c518b84f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "37\\,563" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287902} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a85cb6-5cf8-590a-ba94-3f56b960b346" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f43e163b-14d4-5f29-a377-eb9e20b77aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120626" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation  $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{2}{3}$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(-\\frac{3}{2})=-(56.309\\,9…)^{∘}≈-{56.310}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-{56.310}^{∘}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}-{56.310}^{∘}={123.690}^{∘},\\,\\,{x}_{2}={360}^{∘}+x={360}^{∘}-{56.310}^{∘}={303.690}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n123.690\\cdot 303.690≈37\\,563\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c71c49ee-e496-5d4e-87fa-96e28dd830ca" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cotangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5883a09-7c42-552f-b4fe-2e0163e8c270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287907} {:answer/id #uuid "2965aeaf-0e95-59fd-8ebe-ffaff20a8dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2965aeaf-0e95-59fd-8ebe-ffaff20a8dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287908} :answer-field/id #uuid "302f74cc-153e-5c40-9456-58665a27d091" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ace6c7bf-8a1b-5f25-8196-dd5768c28aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "243" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace6c7bf-8a1b-5f25-8196-dd5768c28aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "243" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287910} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b744595-480c-5bf3-b48d-25f42ec751ff" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ed1c596-9728-51d1-9ce6-4b4e58954fb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-274561" :question/problem "Find, **in ascending order and rounded to the nearest integer**, the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$  for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$ and $x=$ \n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)=(63.434\\,9…)^{∘}≈{63.435}^{∘}\n$$\n\nSince ${63.435}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution, rounded to the nearest integer, is ${x}_{1}={63}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$\nHence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+x={180}^{∘}+{63.435}^{∘}≈{243}^{∘},\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x={63}^{∘}$ and $x={243}^{∘}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74c9c0f6-034c-5d9c-935a-ca27dec1a648" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Cotangent Under a Modified Domain"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bc1e540-8ee5-526e-b476-882f5edfe7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc1e540-8ee5-526e-b476-882f5edfe7a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287913} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef20d2ee-3068-5877-9e89-41f18a25dfa2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffe61de-9801-53a1-8861-019d7fe8180f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ffe61de-9801-53a1-8861-019d7fe8180f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287915} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f8ad7e-daa7-541e-ab4b-ea2292adbab1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c031cfa-13ed-5750-8fa4-f8a5e9a5765e" :question/math-academy-id "q-330609" :question/problem "Find the two solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ for $-\\pi <x<\\pi .$\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$ \n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies in the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add or subtract integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =(-2)\\cdot \\pi +x=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3}=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e126b20-0507-5f22-ba34-a55157ca7fa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation When the Cotangent Function Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74bbe537-0393-5197-93c9-2d60008d0431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287918} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad5e99a-ed6f-5906-ac8f-2c9367c35251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287919} {:answer/id #uuid "d77aa76e-58c5-547b-8932-62592889bbef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287920} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a94f28-0536-52d2-a217-6dea9d6ce0c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287921} {:answer/id #uuid "86faa83b-6ba5-5224-9e36-bc20a3994ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad5e99a-ed6f-5906-ac8f-2c9367c35251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287919} :answer-field/id #uuid "d60cb6f7-f0a2-50ee-b9c1-48b1dcdd1445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287917}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7efbc2c8-eaf3-59d3-ac9a-ab6526fedd99" :question/math-academy-id "q-80193" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $4=4-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{2}$ for $-2\\pi <x<0,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =4-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{2} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ lies outside the given domain, it is not a solution.\n\nTo find more solutions, we subtract integer multiples of $\\pi $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-\\pi +x=-\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-2\\pi +x=-2\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our solutions are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e126b20-0507-5f22-ba34-a55157ca7fa1" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation When the Cotangent Function Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff90101b-5754-5d9f-9563-3d35a247e18e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287925} {:answer/id #uuid "067fce08-834f-5ba1-adfc-c279a230df12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287926} {:answer/id #uuid "28a509ea-f23e-569a-880d-3d1ae26854fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16\\,200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287927} {:answer/id #uuid "fe93438d-d43d-53e7-ad22-025c93d4060e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287928} {:answer/id #uuid "f2875082-9372-54e8-b87f-6cb0208b210f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24\\,300" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "067fce08-834f-5ba1-adfc-c279a230df12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\,100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287926} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e4367d-682c-5be9-9f1b-28a77c4788e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "936da1a3-12b9-5773-8bc1-7b9d9679b27f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80197" :question/problem "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $2=2-9\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation to isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =2-9\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ 0 & =-9\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't find an equivalent equation involving tangent, since this would lead to us dividing by $0:$\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{1}{0}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can instead find an equivalent equation using the fact that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=0\n$$\n\nIn this case, we can find the principal solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =0 \\\\ x & =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡0 \\\\ x & ={90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value lies inside the desired domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{∘}.$\n\nTo find more solutions, we subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & ={90}^{∘}-{180}^{∘} \\\\  & =-{90}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our solutions are $x=-{90}^{∘},{90}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n90\\cdot (-90)=-8\\,100.\n$$"}]}
